nother actor an action that loads goods onto the carrier, or let the carrier pick them up itself). A process may renew raw materials at their source or bring new demand, but never supply what an action makes or move goods between places. In the 24-round test these moves were never possible for anyone: deliver-boxes (The source has enough packed pencils: was 0, needed 1; stock.packed_pencils is raised only by pack-pencils (on its actor)); sell-pencils (The shop has the requested pencils: was 0, needed 1; stock.pencils is raised only by assemble-pencils (on its actor)). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that brings them there). These moves use up a good where it never arrives, so they can never happen: sell-pencils needs pencils at shop, which starts with none and nothing ever gives it any. Give the holder a source: the step that makes or carries the good must add it there (a delivery that counts down must add the goods to the receiver when it ends). Rules can only change the actor and the entities its fields name, and cannot add actions or fields. Return a corrected structure (JSON object only) whose actions and fields let every step and every actor happen, keeping what already worked."}]

